<title>GERMANY: German inland gas oil still facing slow buying.</title>
<headline>German inland gas oil still facing slow buying.</headline>
<text>
<p>(DLR/DM=1.6808)   DM/100 LTRS     DLRS/100 LTRS   LAST DM</p>
<p>HAMBURG	     36.40/36.80     21.65/21.89     35.80/36.30</p>
<p>BREMEN		36.40/36.80     21.65/21.89     35.80/36.30</p>
<p>DUISBURG	    36.50/36.90     21.72/21.95     36.40/36.70</p>
<p>FRANKFURT	   37.00/37.50     22.01/22.31     36.50/36.80</p>
<p>KARLSRUHE	   36.80/37.20     21.89/22.13     36.60/37.00</p>
<p>INGOLSTADT	  38.80/39.10     23.08/23.26     37.90/38.30</p>
<p>German inland gas oil continued to be poorly sought on Wednesday with the mild weather prompting buyers to question whether they need material at current prices. &quot;There is little urgency so maybe people are waiting, &quot; said one trader.</p>
</text>
